From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:03:57 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: Set the keepalive thresholds as macOS does

Region C +0x7f4 and +0x7f8 are the keepalive performance and off-mode
thresholds, in hundredths of a state. The driver left them zero; macOS
26.6.2 sets 100 on the J713 (captured by Niklas Sheth). The meaning is
from interface notes by Syd Garlathy <s@ll.dev>, written from macOS's
drivers. No difference in rendering or idle was measured.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Youwes09 <yuvi.shen@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs
index a871d9812eac..414e896e06cc 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16_platform.rs
@@ -424,6 +424,10 @@ pub(crate) fn region_c(&self) -> Result<KVec<u8>> {
             (0x9c8, 40),
             (0x9cc, 50),
             (0x9d0, 1),
+            // Keepalive performance and off-mode thresholds, in hundredths
+            // of a state.
+            (0x7f4, 100),
+            (0x7f8, 100),
             (0x84, self.maximum_power),
             (0x88, top_state),
             (0x8c, top_state),
